# --- Original media, firmware, and third-party SDK archives: never committed ---
# Apple ROMs, Berkeley Systems' modules and SDKs, and disk images are someone
# else's copyrighted material. The whole folder is a local-only cache so they
# don't have to be re-downloaded or re-extracted — see reference/README.md and
# the main README's "Reference materials" section for how to reconstitute it.
/reference/
*.ROM
Old_World_Mac_Roms.zip
New_World_Mac_Roms.zip

# The source disk image and anything extracted from it.
AfterDark-original.img
*.img
!fixtures/**/*.img

# Extracted original assets and generated module packs. No exceptions: an
# earlier version of this file whitelisted `dist/**/*.rsrc` so the packaged app
# could carry a playable library, which committed 55 Berkeley Systems modules
# and Apple's fonts to a public repository. The app now imports them from the
# user's own disk at first launch instead.
/modules/
**/forks/
*.rsrc

# Oracle captures (large, regenerable; commit hashes not frames).
/tests/oracle/captures/

# --- Build output ---
# dist/ IS ignored, and used to not be. It held the packaged macOS bundles,
# which is how the download the README linked to was published — ~8 MB of binary
# committed afresh on every rebuild, permanently, for a file that is a pure
# function of the commit it was built from. The downloads are GitHub Release
# assets now, built by .github/workflows/release.yml on a version tag; this is
# where make_app.sh and make_dist.sh leave their output locally.
/dist/
/target/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# --- Scratch ---
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# repomix generates a full-repo dump; useful locally, never in history
repomix-output.xml
trapscan.json

# Disc images: Berkeley Systems' software, not this project's.
*.iso
*.iso.zip
